{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I’ll be helping take care of you during this stay. How are you feeling right now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. Honestly, I’m exhausted. I’ve been vomiting nonstop—like a liter or more every day. I feel so weak and dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. The team told me you’ve lost about 13 pounds since your last discharge. That’s significant. We’ve started you on IV fluids to help rehydrate you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been trying to keep track in my intake/output diary. It’s been negative for over a week. I just can’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We checked your labs, and your kidney function was a bit off when you came in—creatinine was 1.3—but it’s already improving with fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? My kidneys were bad last time too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was mild this time, likely from dehydration. With fluids, it’s already coming back to normal. We’re watching it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. I’m just so tired of being in and out of the hospital for this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. You’ve been through a lot. We’re continuing your usual nausea meds—promethazine and octreotide—and added IV Phenergan and lorazepam since you said they work better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the IV ones help more. The oral ones don’t stay down long enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll keep using IV as needed. Your G-tube is still working well for decompression, so that’s helping too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I wish I could just get IV fluids at home. I wouldn’t have to keep coming back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. Dr. Patel mentioned you’re still working on insurance approval for home IV or TPN. You may need to complete some paperwork to help with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been trying, but it’s so frustrating. No one seems to follow through."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2185-03-27 18:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have social work check in with you. They might be able to help coordinate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs this morning look much better—creatinine is down to 0.9, and your electrolytes are stabilizing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I only threw up once last night. I think the fluids are helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and your weight is stable at 155 pounds. That’s a good sign you’re not losing more fluid than you’re taking in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was worried I’d lost more. My home scale said 143, but I guess it’s not accurate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hospital scales are more reliable. And your albumin is 4.4, which means your nutrition is holding up despite the vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I’ve been eating when I can—bacon, eggs, fries. I know it’s not healthy, but it’s what I can keep down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’ve heard the nurses mention that. Fatty foods might actually make nausea worse for some people. Have you tried smaller, lighter meals?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really. I get so hungry when I’m not vomiting, I just eat whatever I want."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I get that. But maybe we could try something like toast, crackers, or broth between meals. It might help reduce nausea long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can try. But I don’t want to feel hungrier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2185-03-28 07:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work with nutrition to suggest some options. Small, frequent meals might help balance that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2185-03-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the pain today? Still around your abdomen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2185-03-29 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s constant. It’s not sharp, but it’s there. My usual morphine helps, but sometimes I need more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2185-03-29 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you two doses of IV Dilaudid, and you said it helped. We’ll keep using your home pain plan unless it’s not enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2185-03-29 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s manageable. I just hate feeling like this all the time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2185-03-29 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. Chronic pain is tough. We’ll keep supporting you with meds and comfort measures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2185-03-30 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed you’ve been saying you feel off-balance. Like your feet aren’t hitting the floor right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2185-03-30 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. It’s scary. I’m afraid I’ll fall, especially at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2185-03-30 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your neuro exam was normal—sensation, strength, coordination are all intact. But physical therapy saw you and thinks a walker could help with stability."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2185-03-30 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A walker? I don’t want to seem frail."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2185-03-30 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not about frailty—it’s about safety. You’ll have a visiting nurse come to your home to check for fall risks too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2185-03-30 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, if it helps me stay safe. I do feel better knowing someone will check the house."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2185-03-31 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve gone two full days without vomiting. That’s great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2185-03-31 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still feel nauseous, but I’m keeping fluids down. I even ate some soup yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2185-03-31 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a big improvement. We’re stopping IV fluids now since you’re maintaining hydration on your own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2185-03-31 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does that mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2185-03-31 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge in a day or two. We want to make sure you’re stable and have support at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2185-03-31 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous. Last time, I got dehydrated again within days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2185-03-31 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. That’s why we’re setting up the visiting nurse and encouraging you to follow up with Dr. Patel. We want to catch things early."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2185-04-01 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ECG showed some changes—slower heart rate, more left axis deviation—but it’s stable compared to before. Nothing urgent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2185-04-01 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My heart’s always been fast. It’s usually in the 120s."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2185-04-01 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and now it’s down to 78. That’s probably because you’re better hydrated. We’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2185-04-01 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I do feel less shaky."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2185-04-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re discharging you today. You’ll go home with your usual meds and the visiting nurse visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2185-04-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m glad to be going home, but I’ll miss having help nearby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2185-04-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But you’re stronger now, and we’re setting up support. Call your husband or PCP if you feel worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2185-04-02 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll try those smaller meals. Maybe it’ll help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2185-04-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the spirit. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2185-03-27 18:37:00",
    "admission_end": "2185-04-02 13:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of sclerosing mesenteritis, chronic nausea, and G-tube dependence was admitted for intractable vomiting and dehydration. She had lost weight and had a negative fluid balance for over a week. IV fluids were given, leading to improvement in kidney function and stabilization of weight at approximately 155 pounds. Nausea persisted but vomiting decreased significantly, and she was able to maintain hydration without further IV support. Pain was managed with her home morphine and occasional IV Dilaudid. She reported a sensation of imbalance, prompting a physical therapy evaluation and recommendation for a walker and home safety assessment. Social concerns about lack of support and difficulty obtaining home IV therapy were noted. She was discharged home with visiting nurse services, continued medications, and follow-up plans.",
    "problems": [
      "Dehydration",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Chronic abdominal pain",
      "Abnormality of gait",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Gastrostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
